To automate the detection of Privilege Escalation, your scanner evaluates vertical access control. This occurs when a user with low privileges (such as a standard affiliate partner or forum member) attempts to access administrative functions, directories, or endpoints meant strictly for platform administrators (like managing database records, approving financial payouts, or modifying server variables). [1, 2] 
Under the 1win program rules you shared, Infrastructure-level settings like open ports are out of scope, but application-layer administrative endpoints are highly eligible for top-tier bounties if a low-privilege user can force them to execute actions.
